<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jebel Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Port of Jebel Ali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jebel Ali is a port town on the coast of Dubai in the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>, about 35 kilometres south-west of the city centre. Its deep-water harbour, opened in 1979, is one of the largest man-made harbours in the world and the busiest port in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebel-ali-free-zone">Jebel Ali Free Zone</a>, set up in 1985, drew thousands of foreign companies and was central to Dubai's growth as a trading hub.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jebel-ali.jpg" alt="Jebel Ali" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dennis Sylvester Hurd from Vancouver, Canada · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evening_Two_at_the_Expo_(51733603706).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
